WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.164 --> 00:00:10.514
In tutorial 7.9, you'll choose
what your weekly tracking checks,

00:00:10.564 --> 00:00:13.506
see the credits it uses, and
pause it when you need a break.

00:00:14.536 --> 00:00:18.736
First, open Website settings,
then Tracking & monitors.

00:00:18.786 --> 00:00:23.201
The Weekly tracking card shows what's
connected and how many keywords are tracked.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:28.365
Need a break? Pause stops the
weekly reports, monitors and pages,

00:00:28.415 --> 00:00:29.832
until you start them again.

00:00:31.249 --> 00:00:34.514
Next, scroll to Keywords
and Google Analytics.

00:00:34.564 --> 00:00:39.719
The country is your website's main country;
to change it, use Business details.

00:00:39.769 --> 00:00:41.868
Then type other keywords to watch.

00:00:42.896 --> 00:00:47.991
Add your Google Analytics property ID,
or leave it empty and it's found for you.

00:00:48.041 --> 00:00:52.704
Then save, and a fresh report is
sent. It uses about 6 credits.

00:00:53.745 --> 00:00:58.110
Not sure what to pick? Each field has
a guide, like How do I choose these,

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.217
that walks you through it step by step.

00:01:01.724 --> 00:01:06.574
Now, back at the top, choose how many
pages a week are written for your keyword.

00:01:06.624 --> 00:01:09.038
The credits a month update as you choose.

00:01:10.742 --> 00:01:13.967
If you choose None while a
keyword still has pages to write,

00:01:14.017 --> 00:01:17.067
Check this first tells you
before anything changes.

00:01:17.117 --> 00:01:19.836
Keep 1 page a week, or click Cancel.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.670
Then switch the growth monitors on or off.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.545
In AI visibility, tick Follow my keywords,

00:01:26.595 --> 00:01:29.870
so your AI questions follow
the keywords you work on.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:33.819
The daily check can ask only
those questions, which costs less.

00:01:34.873 --> 00:01:36.793
Next, the backlink monitor,

00:01:36.843 --> 00:01:41.086
the link builder and the monthly technical
audit each have their own switch.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:46.751
For the audit, choose 200,
500 or 1000 pages to check,

00:01:46.801 --> 00:01:49.852
and turn on Render JavaScript
if your site needs it.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:55.035
Add your brand names, so AI answers
and mentions are matched to you,

00:01:55.085 --> 00:01:57.191
and the competitors you
want to compare with.

00:01:59.335 --> 00:02:03.635
Next, Content groups sort your
pages, like blog or services,

00:02:03.685 --> 00:02:06.374
so the weekly report
shows how each group does.

00:02:07.374 --> 00:02:11.499
Click Add a group, give it a name and
the part of the address its pages share,

00:02:11.549 --> 00:02:13.102
then click Save groups.

00:02:15.921 --> 00:02:19.641
Finally, Estimated credits a
month adds up every schedule,

00:02:19.691 --> 00:02:24.246
so you see what each part uses. Click
Save monitors to keep your choices.

00:02:25.424 --> 00:02:27.974
And if a change would
use up your credits fast,

00:02:28.024 --> 00:02:32.524
Check this first says how long they
would last, before anything is saved.

00:02:32.574 --> 00:02:34.857
Click Cancel to keep things as they are.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:39.395
So your weekly tracking checks
exactly what matters to you,

00:02:39.445 --> 00:02:42.056
and you always know the
credits each part uses.

00:02:43.071 --> 00:02:47.321
So, pause when you need to, set
your keywords, choose pages a week,

00:02:47.371 --> 00:02:51.416
switch the monitors, add brands
and competitors, group your pages,

00:02:51.466 --> 00:02:53.453
and check the credits and the warnings.

00:02:54.437 --> 00:02:59.969
Your weekly checks are set. Next, read
your weekly report in tutorial 7.10.
